# Keeps the build context small. `docker/Dockerfile` is the only image that builds from the
# repository root, and its builder stage runs a full Gradle build -- so the context needs the
# sources and nothing else: no history, no local build output, no editor state, and nothing
# belonging to a build that has its own context.
#
# Patterns are `**/`-prefixed on purpose. A single-level `*/build` matches
# `serverpackcreator-api/build` but not `buildSrc/build`.

# History. Nothing in the build reads it -- `docker/Dockerfile` passes `-Pversion` explicitly.
.git
.gitattributes

# Local build output. None of it is an input; `media/` alone is install4j's, and is the largest
# thing in the tree.
**/build
**/out
**/dist
**/.quasar
**/node
**/node_modules
**/tests/
.gradle/
media/

# Editor state, and the GitHub workflows -- which nothing in the build reads.
#
# `.forgejo/` is deliberately NOT here: `buildSrc/build.gradle.kts` declares
# `.forgejo/actions/resolve-version/action.yml` as an input of `:buildSrc:test`, so excluding it
# fails the image build outright with "Input file does not exist". Root `.gitignore` is a declared
# input of `:serverpackcreator-api` for the same reason -- check `inputs.file(` across the build
# before adding anything here.
.idea/
.run/
.vscode/
.github/
.DS_Store

# Has its own context and its own .dockerignore. `docker/Dockerfile` never touches the website,
# and `settings.gradle.kts` does not include it.
serverpackcreator-homepage/

# These describe how to RUN the image; they are not inputs to building it.
docker/docker-compose-dev.yml
docker/docker-compose.yml
